  "solution": {
    "text": "Shortest distance always lies along the common normal<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Slope of common normal is <math><mn>1</mn></math><br />Now, the equation of the normal at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>acos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>bsin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>on</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> where slope is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br />or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(rejected because it gives farthest point)<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Nearest point is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  }
